Add a kbase (non-DRM) dispatch path to pan_kmod_dev_create().

pan_kmod_dev_create() identifies a device by calling drmGetVersion() and
matching the DRM driver name against a table. kbase is a misc character
device (/dev/mali0), not a DRM node, so drmGetVersion() fails on it and the
function bails before any backend is consulted.

This adds a probe for kbase *before* the DRM path, mirroring how Turnip
special-cases kgsl (/dev/kgsl-3d0) alongside DRM enumeration. The probe is
KBASE_IOCTL_VERSION_CHECK, which is side-effect free and fails cleanly on a
non-kbase fd (see pan_kmod_fd_is_kbase() in pan_kmod_kbase.c).

pan_kmod_fd_is_kbase() reports the kbase UK interface version through
out-params rather than having this file issue the ioctl itself, specifically
so that pan_kmod.c - generic, driver-agnostic code - needs no kbase UAPI
headers. That UK version is used as the pan_kmod_driver version, since it is
the closest analogue to a DRM driver version and is what kbase clients
actually version-gate on.

Note the `if (!allocator)` default is hoisted above the probe, because the
kbase path needs the allocator too.

Generated with `diff -u` against Mesa 26.3.0-devel (commit c439d52c) and
verified: both translation units compile clean for aarch64-linux-android26,
and pan_kmod.o's two undefined kbase symbols resolve exactly against
pan_kmod_kbase.o.

--- a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/pan_kmod.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/pan_kmod.c
@@ -14,6 +14,14 @@
 
 extern const struct pan_kmod_ops panfrost_kmod_ops;
 extern const struct pan_kmod_ops panthor_kmod_ops;
+extern const struct pan_kmod_ops kbase_kmod_ops;
+
+/* Defined in pan_kmod_kbase.c. kbase is not a DRM driver, so it cannot be
+ * identified by drmGetVersion() like the backends above. Reports the kbase
+ * UK interface version through out-params so this file needs no kbase UAPI
+ * headers.
+ */
+bool pan_kmod_fd_is_kbase(int fd, uint16_t *uk_major, uint16_t *uk_minor);
 
 static const struct {
    const char *name;
@@ -51,15 +59,34 @@
 pan_kmod_dev_create(int fd, uint32_t flags,
                     const struct pan_kmod_allocator *allocator)
 {
-   drmVersionPtr version = drmGetVersion(fd);
+   drmVersionPtr version;
    struct pan_kmod_dev *dev = NULL;
 
-   if (!version)
-      return NULL;
-
    if (!allocator)
       allocator = &default_allocator;
 
+   /* kbase is not a DRM driver - it's a misc character device (/dev/mali0)
+    * with its own ioctl surface, so drmGetVersion() fails on it. Probe for
+    * it before falling through to DRM enumeration. This mirrors how Turnip
+    * special-cases kgsl (/dev/kgsl-3d0).
+    */
+   uint16_t kbase_uk_major = 0, kbase_uk_minor = 0;
+   if (pan_kmod_fd_is_kbase(fd, &kbase_uk_major, &kbase_uk_minor)) {
+      /* kbase reports a UK interface version rather than a DRM driver
+       * version. Use it as the pan_kmod_driver version so the usual
+       * pan_kmod_driver_version_at_least() gating keeps working.
+       */
+      const struct pan_kmod_driver kbase_drv_info = {
+         .version = {.major = kbase_uk_major, .minor = kbase_uk_minor},
+      };
+
+      return kbase_kmod_ops.dev_create(fd, flags, &kbase_drv_info, allocator);
+   }
+
+   version = drmGetVersion(fd);
+   if (!version)
+      return NULL;
+
